---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" path="/about/"
      description="OpenPRA ORG Inc. is a 501(c)(3) non-profit building open-source probabilistic risk assessment tools and methods.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1 style="max-width:19ch">An instrument, not an authority</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1.1rem">
        OpenPRA ORG Inc. is a 501(c)(3) non-profit. It builds open-source tools
        and methods for probabilistic risk assessment, and gives them away.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem">What we are trying to do</h2>
        <p style="margin-top:.9rem">
          Bring researchers, practitioners, vendors, and regulators into one
          non-competitive space where models, data, and methods can actually be
          inspected. Not because openness is virtuous, but because a risk model
          nobody outside the organisation can read has never really been
          reviewed.
        </p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;margin-top:2rem">What we are not</h2>
        <p style="margin-top:.9rem">
          We do not certify anything, endorse any design, or issue findings. The
          platform quantifies what you give it and shows its working. The
          judgement stays with the analyst and the regulator.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem">How we work</h2>
        <ul style="margin-top:.9rem">
          <li><strong>Transparency and openness.</strong> Data, software, and methods in public, including what does not work yet.</li>
          <li><strong>Collaboration and inclusivity.</strong> A non-competitive space for researchers, industry, and regulators, wherever they are.</li>
          <li><strong>Accessibility.</strong> Everything free and open source. No paid tier.</li>
          <li><strong>Quality and rigour.</strong> Peer review, benchmarks against reference solutions, and stated scope.</li>
          <li><strong>Portability.</strong> Models leave as easily as they arrive.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;margin-top:2rem">Origins</h2>
        <p style="margin-top:.9rem">
          The work grew out of the Probabilistic Risk Assessment Group in the
          Department of Nuclear Engineering at NC State University, and was
          introduced formally at ASME IMECE in 2023. OpenPRA ORG Inc. is a
          separate organisation from any university or company that contributes
          to it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sunken" style="padding-bottom:0">
    <div class="wrap" style="padding-bottom:clamp(3.5rem,8vw,6.5rem)">
      <span class="eyebrow">What we do</span>
      <h2>Three lines of work</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:1.75rem">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Software</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:.5rem">
            Free, open-source PRA software and libraries: a unified analytical
            environment for hybrid models, scalable quantification, and web
            interfaces that let engineers compute and see risk insights without
            installing anything.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Standardisation</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:.5rem">
            Standard data models and formats so different tools interoperate — a
            universal, software-independent representation for PRA models,
            including automatic generation of models from systems engineering
            descriptions (MBSE).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Education and community</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:.5rem">
            Training and outreach for the next generation of practitioners:
            webinars, collaborative forums, classroom use, and worked examples
            anyone can open.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Get involved</span>
      <h2>Ways in</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:1.75rem">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Write code</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:.5rem">TypeScript, C++, or Python. The contribution guide is in the monorepo.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/openpra-org/openpra-monorepo/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contributing guide →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Build models</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:.5rem">Reference models, benchmarks, and worked examples are as valuable as code — and rarer.</p>
          <a href="/models/">Existing models →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Review and document</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:.5rem">Read a schema definition against a standard and tell us where it falls short.</p>
          <a href="mailto:info@openpra.org">info@openpra.org →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:2rem">
        Not a coder? Writing a tutorial, building a worked example, or editing
        the documentation is as useful as a pull request.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sunken" id="contact">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Supporters</span>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem">Thank you</h2>
        <p style="margin-top:.9rem">
          We are grateful to the academic, industry, and government partners who
          support this work, to our funders, and to the wider PRA community for
          the contributions and criticism that shape it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem">Get in touch</h2>
        <p style="margin-top:.9rem">
          <a href="mailto:info@openpra.org">info@openpra.org</a><br />
          <a href="https://github.com/openpra-org">github.com/openpra-org</a>
        </p>
        <p class="note">
          OpenPRA ORG Inc. is recognised as a public charity under section
          170(b)(1)(A)(vi).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
